= Week 12 — Sentimental Things, Saved for Last on Purpose

This is the week we saved for last on purpose. Eleven weeks ago, deciding about a hand towel was not easy. Now you have made hundreds of decisions, and you have space in your home and in your head. That is the right time to open the boxes that hold photos, letters, kids' drawings and things that came from someone you love.

The idea this week is simple: keep the memory, and you may not need to keep every object. A photo and a few written lines can hold a story a box of things cannot. Nothing here is a race, and nothing has to go. Keep is always a fine answer. Sell is there if you want it, and you never have to use it.

Work in 15-minute blocks and stop when the timer rings. If a box feels heavy, close it and come back tomorrow. One rule for the week: if something belongs to another family member, ask before you decide.

